course: dictionary
lesson: 15038
title: Retain: keep it, hold it, remember it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To retain something is to keep it and not lose it or give it away. «Sam kept his receipt so he could retain proof of his purchase.» Here retain means keep.
explain: Retain can also mean to hold something in. A sponge retains water, so it soaks up water and holds it instead of letting it all drip out. A flask retains heat, so your hot drink stays warm for hours.
explain: Retain can mean remember too. «Ava revised her spellings every night, so she could retain them for the test.» When you revise, you help your brain keep what you learned. To check a meaning, swap it into the sentence: if «keep» still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Retain means to keep something and not lose it or give it away.
fact: «Retain» can mean to hold something in, as a sponge retains water.
fact: «Retain» can mean to remember facts, so «retain the facts» means remember them.
fact: Wool and fur retain heat, which is why a warm coat keeps your body warm.
fact: In maths, what you retain is what is left after giving some away: 12 stickers minus 5 given away means you retain 7.
exercise: «Mum asked me to retain the receipt until the toy is checked.» What does retain mean? | *Keep | Give to a friend | Lose | Throw away
exercise: Soil retains water after the rain. What does retains mean here? | Turns the water into ice | Makes the water dirty | Lets all the water run away | *Holds the water in
exercise: Ella had 12 stickers and gave 5 to her friend. How many stickers did she retain? | 12 | 17 | *7 | 5
test: «Sam tried hard to retain the new words he learned in class.» What does retain mean here? | Sell | Forget | Lose | *Remember
test: A flask keeps your drink hot because it retains heat. What does retain mean in this sentence? | Lets heat escape quickly | *Holds heat in | Throws heat away | Makes heat from cold water
exam: Which sentence uses retain to mean remember? | «She lost her purse at the park.» | «The bus is late again.» | «They painted the fence blue.» | *«He tries to retain every fact from his science book.»
